<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating participant selection: from 4,438 NHANES participants, 296 with refusals or \215Don\220t know\216 responses were excluded, leaving 4,142. Multiple imputation handled missing data; final sample remained 4,142.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Flowchart diagram visualizing Mendelian randomization analysis. It depicts genetic instruments \(SNPs\) affecting the exposure \(periodontal disease\), which may influence the outcome \(COPD\), with confounders represented. Assumptions regarding confounders and pathways are listed, along with bidirectional MR analysis methods and sensitivity analysis tools.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic displays subgroups with beta values and 95 percent confidence intervals for various demographic and health characteristics, including p-values for trend and interaction, to evaluate statistical associations across diverse groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Table summarizing Mendelian randomization analyses between periodontal disease and COPD in European and East Asian populations, showing exposure, outcome, number of SNPs, methods, odds ratios with confidence intervals, p-values, and a forest plot chart visualizing effect size estimates across methods.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Panel A and B display microscopic images at ten and twenty times magnification of cells treated with increasing multiplicity of infection \(MOI\) of P. gingivalis and F. nucleatum respectively, compared to control groups. Panel C and D show bar graphs of cell viability percentages over time for each bacterial treatment versus controls. Panels E and F present qPCR results as bar graphs indicating relative mRNA expression of IL6 and IL8 for both bacterial species at multiple MOI. Panels G and H show chemiluminescence immunoassay \(CLIA\) data with bar graphs of IL6 and IL8 protein concentrations, highlighting elevated levels in bacterial treatments compared to controls. Scale bars visible in microscopic images.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Three-panel scientific figure comparing Control, COPD, and COPD plus Periodontitis groups. Panel A shows 3D dental images with visible tooth and jaw differences. Panel B presents lung histology slides, with enlarged views highlighting tissue damage and inflammation increasing from left to right. Panels C through F display bar graphs quantifying statistical differences between groups in CEJ-ABC distance, lung inflammation score, BALF cell counts, and BALF total protein, with higher values in disease groups and significant differences indicated by asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
